{"reference":"Ezekiel 43","book":"Ezekiel","chapter":43,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"interpretive_questions","title":"The Returning Glory","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"The arrival of the glory of the God of Israel at the east-facing gate (vv. 1-5) is set against Ezekiel’s earlier vision of that glory departing from the defiled temple and city in chapters 8–11. Chapter 43 therefore presents the glory’s entrance into the visionary sanctuary as a return. The larger vision of chapters 40–48 continues beyond this scene with a measured sanctuary, its altar and ministers, offerings, land, river, tribes, resident aliens, and a city named YHWH-shammah.","verse_refs":["Ezekiel 43:1-12","Ezekiel 43:1-27"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_ezekiel_043_9bac8a624094584ff19cd514"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}